id: pm-vcs-390t
title: "Phase 4: pm-vcs versions its own source"
description: "The package must track its own source code in pm-vcs alongside git, so the claim that pm-vcs is a working version control system is demonstrated by the repository itself rather than asserted in a README. The self-hosted history ships as a bundle in the repository and a CI gate proves the bundle's tip tree is exactly the source tree, so source cannot change without the pm-vcs history following it."
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:24.621Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:27.188Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: A tracked bundle holds pm-vcs history of pm-vcs's own source; a CI gate fails when the bundle's tip tree differs from the git-tracked source in any byte; the gate re-verifies every object against its own id; the check is deterministic and cannot pass by regenerating the bundle from a dirty tree
